WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.685 --> 00:00:03.935
[Cheering]

00:00:04.907 --> 00:00:06.320
- I feel like the
pressure is just something

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.843
that you worked for.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:11.543
Pressure is gonna come with you
being one of the top players,

00:00:11.543 --> 00:00:13.693
with you being what you worked to be.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.960
You can use it as fuel, or you
can use it as negative energy

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:22.010
and let it be our downfall.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.590
I wonder how people would feel

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.830
if you asked LeBron about pressure.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.920
He went to the league at 18 years old

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.640
and everybody was saying,
“He wasn't gonna be this.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.840
He wasn't gonna be that.”

00:00:35.637 --> 00:00:37.590
It's all on you. It's all mental, really.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:38.435
- [Announcer 1:] Jabari Smith.

00:00:38.435 --> 00:00:39.677
[Sports announcer chatter]

00:00:39.677 --> 00:00:41.254
- [Announcer 2:] Smith, setup three...

00:00:41.254 --> 00:00:42.184
[Squeak of tape rewinding]

00:00:42.184 --> 00:00:43.485
[Sports announcer chatter)

00:00:43.485 --> 00:00:44.995
- [Announcer 3:] He loves his three.

00:00:44.995 --> 00:00:47.125
[Sneakers squeaking)

00:00:47.125 --> 00:00:49.952
[Blues guitar music)

00:00:49.952 --> 00:00:53.780
- 12:27 in the afternoon
when he was born.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.660
Play that number Cash
4 frequently. [Laughing]

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.490
It was what every dad dream about.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.233
Holding his own son, daughter, kid.

00:01:04.265 --> 00:01:06.180
- Basketball really wasn't,
you know, forced upon me.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.290
Like, I really loved basketball as a kid.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.543
Like, I used to be watching the games,

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.430
playing 2K, like, anything.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.593
Basketball was just me.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.180
Just come from an athletic family,

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.513
so it was like, it was kind of natural.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.530
- Well, this what you want
to do? You want to go hoop?

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.700
OK, let me show you
what's going on with this.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.427
Like, OK, this is how you do this.

00:01:27.427 --> 00:01:29.880
And he started—it’s an everyday thing.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.883
Now “Dad, wake me up.” Five years old.

00:01:32.883 --> 00:01:35.147
Like, before the bus come, put
the lights in the driveway,

00:01:35.147 --> 00:01:37.823
turn the garage light
on. Now we got light.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.390
- It kind of, like, felt naturally.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:43.570
My brother playing it. My dad played it.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.530
It's, like, it's just in my household.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.577
So it's, like, it's hard
to say no to it, really.

00:01:49.578 --> 00:01:53.111
[Video reel clicking)

00:01:53.111 --> 00:01:58.111
- So I used to come home
from these overseas jobs.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.690
You gone for five months,

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:02.670
so you ain't laying eyes on your kids.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.643
And my last long stint was Iran.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.480
The boy grew so much.
His brother grew so much.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.380
So, you know, they picked
me up from the airport.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.813
You know, I teared up.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.740
- It was just hard for him to
keep leaving for many months

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.314
and then coming back
and seeing me growing up

00:02:19.314 --> 00:02:20.147
and stuff like that.

00:02:20.147 --> 00:02:21.420
He just didn't really
wanna miss out on that

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:22.590
too much more, so...

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.986
- I wanted to be a daddy
more than I wanted to go hoop

00:02:26.986 --> 00:02:27.823
at that point.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.670
- He could've played basketball
as long as he wanted to,

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:33.820
but he knew as I got older, he
just wanted to be in my life.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.370
Cuz, you know, he grew up
without a father figure.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.517
It was just his focal point
to just be in my life,

00:02:39.517 --> 00:02:41.920
just give me that guidance,
just be there with me

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:42.753
along the way.

00:02:42.753 --> 00:02:44.830
So, I just owe him to give it my all.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.190
He stopped playing basketball for me,

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:47.690
so why wouldn’t I just go out there

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.590
and give it my all, maximize my potential

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:54.090
and just go as far as I want
to with basketball. So...

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.650
- [Interviewer:] Favorite
thing in the room?

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.200
- I got a lot of,

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.340
I got a lot of high school stuff,

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.860
but this is my McDonald's.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:03.380
All of this has kind of
like made me kind of sad.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.230
Cuz, you know, I ain't get to play

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.540
in none of that cuz of
COVID and stuff like that.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.120
But this was the McDonald's
All-American thing.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.580
This was the Jordan Brand Classic.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.740
But they canceled them due
to COVID and stuff like that.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.560
This was my Mr. Georgia Basketball plaque.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.030
Atlanta Celtics jersey.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.370
This is my USA jersey.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:23.560
And this is from, um,
the Battle 4 Atlantis,

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.300
when we went into the Bahamas.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.570
I got All-Tournament Team.

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:28.180
It's got some dust on it.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.700
I really been adding
ever since I got here.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.340
When I first got here, I
didn't have nothing in here.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:32.820
Then I seen everybody
else's room, I'm like,

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.133
hold on, they can't outdo me.

00:03:38.793 --> 00:03:41.850
- You know, Coach Dye, who is a legend

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.320
that we will never be able to replace here

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.420
at Auburn, told me, he said, you know,

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.320
and he's said it before,

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.330
you can coach them as
hard as you love them.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.640
And so I don't love them right away,

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.030
cuz I don't know them right away.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.020
But I get to know them,

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.400
I am honest with them and
I do hold them accountable.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.320
If you had a dad in your life
or an uncle or a grandfather,

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:01.230
you put up with him because
you knew he loved you,

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:02.700
and he held you to account, didn't he?

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.420
And so I hold them to account.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:06.740
- [Jabari Jr.:] Me, when I was
deciding to come to school,

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.520
I wanted to come somewhere
where I was gonna,

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:09.523
I knew I was gonna have fun,

00:04:09.523 --> 00:04:10.916
and I knew I was gonna build relationships

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:12.450
that would last a lifetime.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:15.143
And Auburn's just
really a family atmosphere.

00:04:17.284 --> 00:04:19.240
- It's a small college town.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:20.959
And so kids that come here understand

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:22.503
they're coming here to train.

00:04:22.503 --> 00:04:24.230
They're coming here to learn.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.063
- [Jabari Jr.:] To come here

00:04:25.063 --> 00:04:26.380
just wanting to experience college,

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.180
you know, not going different routes.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.280
Come to school and just play
for a national championship.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.783
Play for a coach that's
coached people like me.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.060
- He wanted to stay close to home.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.320
He wanted his mom and dad to
be able to come see him play.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.120
He wanted his dad to come
into the gym and train him,

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.187
you know, like he had
done, you know, growing up.

00:04:43.187 --> 00:04:45.180
And I got no problem with
guys getting paid when

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.860
they're 18 years old, if
that's what they wanna do—

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.560
go to this league or
that league or whatever.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.843
But, man, they're missing out
a lot by not going to college

00:04:51.843 --> 00:04:53.467
and just having this experience.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:55.660
And I'm telling you right
now, Jabari wouldn't trade

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.900
this year at Auburn for a lot of money.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:58.960
He wouldn't trade it.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.790
That money's down the road,
and he's getting ready for it.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:02.623
- My junior year, I remember,

00:05:02.623 --> 00:05:05.820
I just remember my Auburn visit
when they played Tennessee.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.824
Sold-out crowd, it was loud,

00:05:07.824 --> 00:05:10.180
how free the players were playing,

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.210
how much fun they was having,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.043
how together they were.

00:05:12.043 --> 00:05:13.930
It was just, like, why
wouldn't you wanna play here?

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.043
Why wouldn't you wanna
play in that environment?

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:17.763
Just time flies, really.

00:05:17.763 --> 00:05:19.670
I still remember when I
was sitting right there,

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:23.077
over there, watching the, um,
watching the game thinking,

00:05:23.077 --> 00:05:25.326
"Dang, I wanna, I wanna play in college.

00:05:25.326 --> 00:05:28.030
I wanna play in the SEC. I
wanna play in a game like this."

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.870
Just me being in it now still feels

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.190
kind of unreal a little bit.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.700
Seeing my name on the back of the jersey,

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:33.920
putting on the uniform every night,

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.823
it's just, it still
feel kinda fake to me.

00:05:38.229 --> 00:05:42.095
[Sports announcer chatter]

00:05:42.095 --> 00:05:46.262
[High-intensity motivating music]

00:05:53.141 --> 00:05:55.230
- We're gonna make history.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.610
This team's beating the
best teams in the country.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:00.160
OK? We're gonna build our resume.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:03.500
Kentucky and Alabama
and Gonzaga and Baylor

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.560
and whoever it is, is the
best team in the country?

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.181
All right, we gotta go through them!

00:06:08.181 --> 00:06:10.117
We gotta go through them!

00:06:10.117 --> 00:06:12.623
And they gotta go through us!

00:06:12.623 --> 00:06:14.965
Let's go! Let's go!

00:06:14.965 --> 00:06:16.282
[Clapping]

00:06:16.282 --> 00:06:17.115
They gotta go through us!

00:06:17.115 --> 00:06:19.247
- [Player:] Let's go, Auburn
on three. FLC! One, two, three!

00:06:19.247 --> 00:06:20.317
- [All:] Auburn!

00:06:20.317 --> 00:06:22.137
[Cheering]

00:06:22.137 --> 00:06:25.554
[Laid-back hiphop music]

00:06:27.971 --> 00:06:30.221
[Cheering]

00:06:51.742 --> 00:06:54.725
- [Announcer:] Jabari,
left wing three. Got it!

00:06:54.725 --> 00:06:55.642
Night! Night!

00:07:01.353 --> 00:07:04.900
- [Jabari Sr.:] Man, I want Jabari to
be one of the best guys

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.100
in the community.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:09.160
You know, I want him to
change so many kids' lives.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.880
I want him to be an impact,

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:14.840
preach being a father,
a family man, a husband.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:18.043
I want that to continuously
come out of his mouth.

00:07:21.759 --> 00:07:23.190
- If you tap into the
fact that we’re here

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:25.980
to educate young people and
get them ready for what's next,

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:27.177
that's what I want for Jabari.

00:07:27.177 --> 00:07:29.060
I want to do the best job in this year

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:31.823
to try to prepare him
for what's coming next.

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:34.810
- That's the goal, you
know. Make my family proud,

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:35.923
make my dad proud.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:38.943
You know, make it.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:42.950
I feel like I'm on the
right track to do that.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.867
[Calm piano music]

